+# Fresh isolated `make reproduce` experiment
+
+This workspace creates a deterministic synthetic Git release, captures six
+primary reproductions and six descriptive baseline runs in fresh
+network-disabled containers, independently reruns and verifies every primary
+record, and generates a 1600-by-900 evidence figure.
+
+Prerequisites are Git, a Docker-compatible `docker` CLI, and the official
+`python:3.12.8-bookworm` image already present locally. The experiment never
+pulls an image. Run it with:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m venv .venv
+.venv/bin/pip install matplotlib==3.9.2
+.venv/bin/python run_experiment.py
+```
+
+The immutable image ID is resolved before release creation and written to
+`study_config.json`. Final scalar metrics are in `results.json`; full checks and
+mismatches are in `verification_results.json`.
